# 🎲 Roll The Dice

This project was developed as part of a technical challenge for a junior fullstack position at Directy.

The goal is to simulate dice rolls using a fullstack approach — combining a simple frontend interface with a backend API that processes the logic and returns results.

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- **Frontend:** HTML, CSS, JavaScript (Vanilla)
- **Backend:** Node.js + Express

## 📁 Project Structure

```
roll-the-dice-challenge/
├── backend/           # Node.js API for dice rolling
│   ├── server.js
│   └── package.json
├── frontend/          # HTML/CSS/JS interface
│   ├── index.html
│   ├── script.js
│   └── styles.css
└── README.md          # Project documentation
```

## 🚀 How to Run Locally

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/msma87/roll-the-dice-challenge
cd roll-the-dice-challenge
```

### 2. Start the backend server

```bash
cd backend
npm install
npm start
```

The server will run at: [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000)

### 3. Open the frontend

Use the Live Server extension in VS Code to run `frontend/index.html`, or simply open the file in your browser.

## ✨ Features

- Choose from six different dice types (D4, D6, D8, D10, D12, D20)
- Backend processes the roll and returns a random result
- Simple UI and clean code structure
- Clear separation between client and server logic

